## 1. Auth Flow

### 1.1 POST /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/login

**Request**:
```json
{
  "{{loginField}}": "{{moduleNameLower}}@{{moduleNameLower}}.local",
  "password": "secret"
}
```

**Response 200** — single-level envelope (R-PKG-024 v1.7.0 GA). Payload envuelto en `data`:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Login exitoso.",
  "data": {
    "access_token": "1|abc123...",
    "refresh_token": "2|def456...",
    "token_type": "Bearer",
    "expires_at": "2026-07-12T19:30:00+00:00",
    "{{moduleNameLower}}": { /* AuthResource del usuario */ }
  },
  "debugMsg": []
}
```

> ⚠️ Los tokens (`access_token`, `refresh_token`, `token_type`, `expires_at`) viven en el BODY
> envueltos en `data`, no en HTTP headers. Consumidores que lean de `response.headers` van a
> recibir `undefined`. **Frontend debe parsear `response.data.access_token`**.

**Response 422** (credenciales inválidas):
```json
{
  "message": "The {{loginField}} field is required.",
  "errors": { "{{loginField}}": ["Credenciales inválidas."] }
}
```

### 1.2 POST /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/refresh

**Request**:
```json
{ "refresh_token": "2|def456..." }
```

**Response 200** — single-level envelope:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Access token refrescado.",
  "data": {
    "access_token": "3|ghi789...",
    "token_type": "Bearer",
    "expires_at": "2026-07-12T19:35:00+00:00"
  },
  "debugMsg": []
}
```

**Response 401** (token inválido o expirado).

### 1.3 GET /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/me

**Headers**: `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`

**Response 200** — single-level envelope:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "",
  "data": {
    "id": "uuid",
    /* + todos los profile fields del scope */
    "is_active": true,
    "roles": [
      { "id": 1, "name": "admin" }
    ],
    "abilities": ["Admin.view", "Admin.edit", "roles.view"]
  },
  "debugMsg": []
}
```

### 1.4 POST /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/logout

**Headers**: `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`

**Response 200** — single-level envelope:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Sesión cerrada.",
  "data": null,
  "debugMsg": []
}
```

### 1.5 POST /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/forgot

**Request**:
```json
{ "{{loginField}}": "{{moduleNameLower}}@{{moduleNameLower}}.local" }
```

**Response 200** (siempre, sin revelar si el email existe) — single-level envelope:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Si el {{loginField}} existe, recibirás un enlace para reset.",
  "data": null,
  "debugMsg": []
}
```

### 1.6 POST /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/reset

**Request**:
```json
{
  "{{loginField}}": "{{moduleNameLower}}@{{moduleNameLower}}.local",
  "token": "raw-token-from-email",
  "password": "new-password-123",
  "password_confirmation": "new-password-123"
}
```

**Response 200** — single-level envelope:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Contraseña actualizada. Iniciá sesión nuevamente.",
  "data": null,
  "debugMsg": []
}
```

**Response 422** (token inválido o expirado > 60min).

> ⚠️ El endpoint `POST /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/register` (R-PKG-027) está pineado con
> `mk.auth:{{moduleNameLower}}` + `mk.ability:{{moduleNameLower}}.{{moduleNamePluralLower}}.create`
> (defense-in-depth per HALLAZGO-NEW-FASE18-C). NO es público por default — para invocarlo
> necesitás un token de admin/{{moduleNameLower}} con ability `{{moduleNamePluralLower}}.create`.

